  "coverage": {
    "batchPreflight": "Three malformed/missing/proxy transport factory refusals occur without invoking their getter/proxy. A duplicate-key batch is rejected before custody, intent or transport writes; no single-submit method is exposed.",
    "sequentialBatch": "Two original requests use the same declared funding pair and execute in order through the actual local backend. Each transport call observes prior native custody and intent write/readback confirmation. The core closes once after both callbacks complete.",
    "retainedOriginalReopen": "Normal native reopen reads both exact originals and cached backend assertions without dispatch or backend mutation. A batch whose first original is already retained is refused before transport; its tail is not retained or attempted.",
    "unknownFirst": "The actual backend commits a success before the declared response is dropped. The runner fails on the first entry, retains client submission uncertainty and releases queued references without launching the tail. The native payer close returns exactly once, while the root's child-unknown close Promise deliberately rejects.",
    "unknownReopen": "After normal same-process reopen, the persisted original and intent still refuse the same first request before transport. A cached backend result remains non-authoritative and deliveryConfirmed false; the tail is not automatically resumed.",
    "uncertaintyLimit": "The prior live client's in-memory submission flag is not a durable transport receipt. This selection does not establish fresh-process recovery or durable reconstruction of response uncertainty.",
    "manualClose": "During one held actual backend callback, a combined read is BUSY before a query and does not poison the connection. Close fences the queued next request and combined reads synchronously. It remains pending until the fixture explicitly releases the active callback, then native close returns once. The batch rejects CLOSE_REQUESTED with one completed and one unattempted original.",
    "teardownSource": "The selected draft now fences queued-next in finally before releasing the held callback and observes the actual run/close/handler promises. No injected failing-assertion branch or cancellation guarantee is claimed.",
    "expectedConfigurationRefusals": [
      "missing explicit transport",
      "accessor transport without invoking its getter",
      "proxy transport without invoking it"
    ],
